# tools/shape_classify_witness.rish -- NAME an unknown shape by the closest of a labeled template library, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/hu_moments.rye reads a component's SEVEN HU INVARIANT MOMENTS (the turn-and-scale
# fingerprint); image/shape_match.rye reads the DISTANCE between two such fingerprints (one scalar, small for the same form). A
# distance answers "are THESE two the same shape?"; a surface asks the next question up: "WHICH of the shapes I know is this?"
# This rung reads that -- the NEAREST-TEMPLATE classifier, the argmin of the distance over a labeled set of known fingerprints.
# Give it an unknown mark's Hu set and a small library of named templates, and it names the class of the closest one, with an
# honest MARGIN (the gap to the runner-up). That is the move a text reader, an icon matcher, and a part recognizer are built on:
# not the distance between two marks, but the CHOICE of the one known form an unknown mark most resembles. Compose not braid:
# this rung owns only the argmin and its margin; shape_match owns the metric, hu_moments the fingerprints, label the LabelMap.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a chiral right triangle turned 90 degrees, mirrored, AND scaled up 4x -- a pose the
# library never saw -- is named the triangle class over a plus, a block, and an L, with a distance under 0.2 and a margin more
# than ten times that (the nearest decoy an order of magnitude farther), so one choice tells which KNOWN form an unknown mark is.
# An unknown that IS a template reads distance exactly zero and names it; a single-template library always wins with a zero
# margin. The decisive ORIENTED-vs-BLIND chirality crux: with a chiral shape AND its mirror as two classes, the reflection-blind
# classifier reads a mirror mark as indistinguishable from both (both distances and the margin under 1e-8) while the oriented
# classifier names the correct handed class a real margin away -- the seventh Hu invariant's sign-flip surfacing as the right
# label. An empty library refuses EmptyTemplates and an over-long one TooManyTemplates. No network, no key, no funds -- the
# "which known shape is this?" a surface asks the moment it has a fingerprint and a library, on our own open geometry.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/shape_classify_witness.rish

say "shape_classify: Language EN -- Season G nearest-template classifier over a labeled library of HuSet fingerprints; classify is the argmin of shape_match's reflection-invariant distance (a mark and its mirror name one class), classify_oriented the argmin of the oriented distance (a chiral mark names its own-handed class), each returning the winner's class id, index, distance, and the margin to the runner-up."
say "shape_classify: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: owns only the argmin and its margin; shape_match owns the metric it minimizes, hu_moments the invariants, label the LabelMap. No pixel read, no image written, no codec touched -- a pure reduction over a slice of seven-number fingerprints."
say "shape_classify: Lens TAME -- the template library is bounded by shape_classify_max_templates (256) so a scan is always finite; an empty library refuses EmptyTemplates and an over-long one TooManyTemplates, each having chosen nothing; ties fall to the earliest template so the choice is deterministic; the distances run in f64 exactly as the metric beneath reads them; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/shape_classify"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/shape_classify.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "shape_classify: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "shape_classify: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "shape_classify: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-shape-classify" else "shape_classify: selftest did not print the GREEN line"

say "shape_classify: GREEN -- a chiral triangle turned, mirrored, and scaled up is named the triangle class over a plus, a block, and an L with a wide margin (the recognition loop closed), an exact template reads distance zero and names itself, a single-template library wins with a zero margin, and the oriented classifier names a mirror mark its correct handed class where the blind one cannot separate the two, on metal."
